This project details the creation of a Question Answering (QA) system operating in Portuguese, processing datasets related to restaurants, hotels, and local attractions in Coimbra. The development progressed through three phases: initially building a rule-based chatbot for semantic extraction, followed by the integration of unsupervised Machine Learning models (K-Means, SVM, LDA) operating on TF-IDF vectorized text to cluster and evaluate responses. The final application features a graphical user interface (via easygui) that prompts users for queries and generates responses using multiple pre-trained transformer models (e.g., T5, BERT, DeBERTa). System performance is rigorously assessed using metrics such as precision, recall, F1-score, accuracy, cosine similarity, and silhouette scores to evaluate both the generated text and the clustering quality.
